multTableOneOne -- the multiplication table for products of elements in degree one
**********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        multTableOneOne A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, created with *note
        resLengthThreeAlg: resLengthThreeAlg, or *note resLengthThreeTorAlg:
        resLengthThreeTorAlg,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Compact: multTableOneOne_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCompact=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value false, an optional argument for multTableOneOne that
        prints dots below the diagonal
      * *note Labels: multTableOneOne_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLabels=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value true, an optional argument for multTableOneOne
        determining whether to label rows and columns
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of the rows in the multiplication
        table; use *note netList: (Macaulay2Doc)netList, to display it as a
        table

Description
===========

For a free resolution of length three described as a graded-commutative ring A,
the function returns a list of the rows of the multiplication table of elements
in degree one. It also computes the multiplication table for products of
elements in degree one in the graded-commutative homology algebra obtained from
A.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = QQ[x,y,z];                                                         |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = resLengthThreeAlg freeResolution ideal (x^2,y^2,z^2)               |
|                                                                            |
|o2 = A                                                                      |
|                                                                            |
|o2 : QuotientRing                                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : multTableOneOne A                                                      |
|                                                                            |
|o3 = {{ , e , e , e }, {e , 0, f , f }, {e , -f , 0, f }, {e , -f , -f , 0}}|
|           1   2   3     1      1   2     2    1      3     3    2    3     |
|                                                                            |
|o3 : List                                                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : netList multTableOneOne A                                              |
|                                                                            |
|     +--+---+---+--+                                                        |
|o4 = |  |e  |e  |e |                                                        |
|     |  | 1 | 2 | 3|                                                        |
|     +--+---+---+--+                                                        |
|     |e |0  |f  |f |                                                        |
|     | 1|   | 1 | 2|                                                        |
|     +--+---+---+--+                                                        |
|     |e |-f |0  |f |                                                        |
|     | 2|  1|   | 3|                                                        |
|     +--+---+---+--+                                                        |
|     |e |-f |-f |0 |                                                        |
|     | 3|  2|  3|  |                                                        |
|     +--+---+---+--+                                                        |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

