multTableOneTwo -- the multiplication table for products of elements in degree one with elements in degree two
**************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        multTableOneTwo A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, created with *note
        resLengthThreeAlg: resLengthThreeAlg, or *note resLengthThreeTorAlg:
        resLengthThreeTorAlg,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Labels: multTableOneTwo_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLabels=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value true, an optional argument for multTableOneTwo
        determining whether to label rows and columns
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of the rows in the multiplication
        table; use *note netList: (Macaulay2Doc)netList, to display it as a
        table

Description
===========

For a free resolution of length three described as a graded-commutative ring A,
the function returns a list of the rows of the multiplication table of elements
in degree one with elements in degree two. It also computes the multiplication
table for products of elements in degree one with elements in degree two in the
graded-commutative homology algebra obtained from A.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = QQ[x,y,z];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = resLengthThreeAlg freeResolution ideal (x^2,y^2,z^2)          |
|                                                                       |
|o2 = A                                                                 |
|                                                                       |
|o2 : QuotientRing                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : multTableOneTwo A                                                 |
|                                                                       |
|o3 = {{0, f , f , f }, {e , 0, 0, g }, {e , 0, -g , 0}, {e , g , 0, 0}}|
|           1   2   3     1         1     2       1        3   1        |
|                                                                       |
|o3 : List                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : netList multTableOneTwo A                                         |
|                                                                       |
|     +--+--+---+--+                                                    |
|o4 = |0 |f |f  |f |                                                    |
|     |  | 1| 2 | 3|                                                    |
|     +--+--+---+--+                                                    |
|     |e |0 |0  |g |                                                    |
|     | 1|  |   | 1|                                                    |
|     +--+--+---+--+                                                    |
|     |e |0 |-g |0 |                                                    |
|     | 2|  |  1|  |                                                    |
|     +--+--+---+--+                                                    |
|     |e |g |0  |0 |                                                    |
|     | 3| 1|   |  |                                                    |
|     +--+--+---+--+                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

