resLengthThreeTorAlg -- the Tor algebra presented as a graded-commutative ring
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        resLengthThreeTorAlg F, resLengthThreeTorAlg(F,L)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a length three free resolution
        of a cyclic module
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of three symbols
  * Outputs:
      * a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, the Tor algebra
        presented as a quotient of a graded-commutative free algebra over the
        residue field of the ambient ring

Description
===========

For a free resolution F over a ring Q, the function returns the algebra
$Tor^Q(R,k)$  as a quotient of a graded-commutative free algebra over the
residue field of Q. The basis vectors in degrees 1, 2, and 3 are named with the
symbols from the list L. The default symbols are e, f, and g.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = QQ[x,y,z];                                             |
